The Z-matrix for the sos-fep calculation needs to be called fepzmat. Then,
to execute an entire sos-fep calculation in water with T=25C and #waters=500,
just enter
csh soscmd11 >& log &

xSOSAQ11 provides a convenient way to run a single fep calculation
in any directory. Runs 11 FEP windows (delta lambda = 0.10). 
This is recommended for general use when addding/removing
zero or one non-H atom.
PhXaq11 contains input files for PhX -> PhY perturbations.
See SOSgas for the corresponding gas-phase perturbations.

xSOSAQ13 uses 13 windows; the first and last window use 
delta lambda = 0.05. 

xSOSAQ15 uses 15 windows; the first two and last two windows  
use delta lambda = 0.05. 

For sos, all increments have to be run forward and backward.

For the Yale queuing system:
xSOSAQQ6     -  6 windows (delta lambda = 0.20)
xSOSAQQ8     -  8 windows 
xSOSAQQ11    - 11 windows (delta lambda = 0.10) 
xSOSAQQ13    - 13 windows 
xSOSAQQ15    - 15 windows 
xSOSAQQ21    - 21 windows (delta lambda = 0.05)

Note: FEP with double-wide sampling and SOS calculations use
unique x-scripts since the schedule of lambda values is different.

xDELGSOS is used to collect and sum the free-energy results;
the final results are in sumout. 
